# Documentation & Readability

- Keep code self-explanatory through naming and structure first.
- Add brief comments only when logic is non-obvious.

## Regex Rule (Mandatory)

- Every regular expression must be preceded by a comment that explains:
  - What the pattern is intended to match
  - Why this pattern is needed
- For complex expressions, include short examples of:
  - Matching strings
  - Non-matching strings

## Example

```ts
// Match ISO dates in YYYY-MM-DD format used by report filters.
// Matches: "2026-05-04"
// Does not match: "04-05-2026", "2026/05/04"
const isoDateRegex = /^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$/;
```
